length:
To-day is not enough or yesterday: God sees it all--
Your length on sunny lawns, the wakeful rainy nights--; tell me--;
(how vain to ask),

lenses:
He looms above the sordid crowd--
At least through friendly lenses;
While his mamma looks pleased and proud,

lends:
In silence be,
When Nature lends her voice to praises;
When heaven and earth

Many a bard's untimely death
Lends unto his verses breath;
Here's a song was never sung:

lens:
Upon my mind
Turn thy pure lens;
Naught shalt thou find

lengthening:
Next you should sit and I would sing
Through lengthening days of sunny spring;
Till, if you wearied of the task,

lentils:
For instance, compromise the wheaten bread
For rye, the meat for lentils, silk for serge,
And sleep on down, if needs, for sleep on straw;
